\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. The God of Abraham praise,
\par Who reigns enthroned above,
\par Ancient of everlasting days,
\par And God of love.
\par Jehovah   Great I AM!
\par By earth and heaven  confessed;
\par I bow and bless the sacred name
\par For ever blessed.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. The God of Abraham praise,
\par At whose supreme command
\par From earth I rise, and seek the joys
\par At His right hand.
\par I all on earth forsake-
\par Its wisdom, fame and power-
\par And Him my only portion make
\par My shield and tower.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. The God of Abraham praise,
\par Whose all -sufficient grace
\par Shall guide me all my happy days
\par In all my ways.
\par He calls a worm His friend,
\par He calls Himself my God;
\par And He shall save me to the end
\par Through Jesu's blood.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. He by Himself hath sworn,
\par I on His oath depend;
\par I shall on eagles' wing upborne,
\par To heaven ascend;
\par I shall behold His face,
\par I shall His power adore,
\par And sing the wonders of His grace
\par For evermore.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Though nature's strength decay,
\par And earth and hell withstand,
\par To Canaan's bounds I urge my way
\par At His command.
\par The watery deep I pass,
\par With Jesus in my view;
\par And through the howling wilderness
\par My way pursue.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. The goodly land I see,
\par With peace and plenty blest,
\par A land of  sacred liberty
\par An endless rest;
\par There milk and honey flow,
\par And oil and wine abound,
\par And trees of life for ever grow,
\par With mercy crowned.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. There dwells the Lord our King,
\par The Lord our Righteousness
\par Triumphant o'er the world and sin,
\par The Prince of  Peace.
\par On Zions sacred height
\par His kingdom still maintains,
\par And glorious with His saints in light
\par For ever reigns.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 8\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 8. He keeps His own secure,
\par He guards them by His side,
\par Arrays in garments white and pure
\par His spotless bride;
\par With streams of sacred bliss,
\par With groves of living joys;
\par With all the fruits of paradise,
\par He still supplies.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 9\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 9. Before the great Three-one
\par They all exulting stand,
\par And tell the wonders He hath done,
\par Through all their land;
\par The listening spheres attend,
\par And swell the growing fame;
\par And sing, in songs which never end,
\par The wondrous name.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 10\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 10. The God who reigns on high,
\par The great archangels sing;
\par And holy, holy, holy, cry,
\par Almighty King,
\par Who was and is the same,
\par And evermore shall be
\par Jehovah, Father, Great I AM,
\par We worship Thee.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 11\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 11. Before the Saviour's face
\par The ransomed nations bow;
\par O'erwhelmed at His mighty grace,
\par For ever new;
\par He shows His prints of love,
\par They kindled to a flame,
\par And sound through all the worlds above
\par The slaughtered Lamb.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 12\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 12. The whole triumphant host,
\par Give thanks to God on high,
\par Hail Father, Son and Holy ghost
\par They ever cry.
\par Hail Abraham's God and  mine
\par I join heavenly lays
\par All might and majesty are Thine,
\par And endless praise.
\par                       Amen.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs16 
\par }

